  "steps": [
    "100g boiled or canned rajma (kidney beans), 100g cooked rice, 100g air fried low fat paneer, 1/2 onion (70g), 1/2 tomato (70g), 1/2 cucumber (70g), 100g greek yogurt, A handful of coriander leaves (around 10-14g), 1 tsp rajma masala, 1/2 tsp cumin powder, 1/2 chilli flakes (adjust as per taste), 1/2 salt (adjust as per taste), 1/2 tsp pepper, Squeeze of 1/2 lime.",
    "To make the air-fried paneer - I marinated the paneer with 1.5 tsp tandoori masala, 1 tbsp Greek yogurt, ½ tsp, and ½ tsp chilli powder, then air-fried it at 200°C for 15 minutes (flip it half way)",
    "If you’re using boiled rajma - soak the dry rajma overnight or for at least 8 hours. Then pressure cook it with salt for 30 minutes."
